opennyai_summary.decision:
The prayers in all these petitions being similar, for convenience we refer to the prayers made in the first petition being Writ Petition No.13634 of 2025, which read thus :
 "(a) Issue appropriate Writ / Order for directing the Respondents to  immediately grant amount of Solatium @ 30% along with interest in  addition to the amount of compensation, with regard to the land belonging  to the Petitioner having an area admeasuring 550 sq. mtrs. from Survey  No.88/2 situated at Village Velholi Taluka and District Nashik, in  accordance with law laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Union of  India v. Tarsem Singh (2019) 9 SCC 304 case, which is followed by the  Divisional Benches of this Hon'ble High Court, (which are annexed at  Exhibit-"C" Collectively)."
Such amounts be deposited within a period of six weeks from the date of receipt of computation from the Competent Authority no.2/Respondent no.4;
(iv) The Competent Authority thereafter shall proceed to disburse the amounts to the Petitioners as would be received from the Project Director, NHAI/acquiring body;
(v) All contentions of parties are expressly kept open;
(vi) The petitions stand disposed of in above terms.
9. At this stage Mr. Singh submitted that the order ought not to be given effect to till the review petition is decided by the Supreme Court.
The request is rejected."
(supra) in terms of the following order:-:
